# Implement gate (repo delta)

Universal authorize / Plan-UI / undo / git gates: User Rule **Collaboration standards** (and **Git — operator only**). Those win.

Authorize product edits only with operator chat verbs **`implement`** or **`patch`**. Plan cards / attached plans do not count.

## Product in this repo

Do not edit until authorized above — includes **all** of:

- Python, JS, HTML, CSS, YAML runtime config, SQL, shell/PowerShell
- **`helpers/**`** scouts/scripts and other executable or runtime artifacts
- Markup that ships with the product

## Pipeline docs (this repo)

- **triage** / **kickoff**: may edit `docs/todo/*` only — no product code, no `helpers/**`.
- Product docs under `docs/**` outside `todo/` only when the operator explicitly asks for a docs change (still no code without `implement` / `patch`).
- **implement** / **patch**: product code + helpers allowed; pipeline close-out when ship/DoD says so (`ship` is docs/close-out language, not a code authorize verb).
- Phase close-out: move Done `docs/todo/phase*.md` → `docs/todo/_archive/` — [`.cursor/rules/phase-archive.mdc`](phase-archive.mdc).

## When unsure

Stop and ask: **triage**, **kickoff**, **implement**, or **patch**? Do not start coding.
